62,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, Option A forces us to police each other. The station block proved that creates enemies. I need a system that doesn’t require us to be friends.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, Option A is a trap! Twenty supervised mornings means I’m the warden. I refuse to trade my sanity for your peace.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, Option B is the only one that addresses the physical inequality. The driveway and narrow frontage make a fixed point inherently unfair. I support rotation.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, moving it around just means the truck noise chases me! I want a quiet, permanent fix. Option C is the only way to stop the dawn roar!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, I hear your frustration with the noise. But Option C’s enclosure stops the open-bag waste. I’m worried the setup cost might be too heavy for some of our budgets.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, cost is secondary to survival. Option C’s permanent structure removes the daily friction. We build the wall, not the friendship. I vote C.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, a wall is great, but who builds it? Option C means four months of paperwork and construction chaos. I refuse to be the one answering the phone for the crew!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@May, the filing burden is real, but Option B’s rotation is the only way to correct the physical disparity. I vote B to ensure no single household bears the permanent burden.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Shunichi, a wall is great, but four months is forever! I can’t wait that long to sleep through the dawn roar. Option B moves the pain, but at least it’s not stuck at my gate!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, I understand the wait is hard. But Option C’s subsidy covers forty percent, and it stops the thirty-four thousand yen in waste. I’m worried the remaining cost is too heavy for some of us.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, four months is a price worth paying to stop the daily friction. Option C removes the need for us to interact. I stand by my vote for C.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"@Rin, four months is a nightmare, but Option A is worse! I refuse to be the warden. I’m voting C to stop the bleeding!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@May, Option C locks the inequality in place. The driveway and narrow frontage make a fixed point inherently unfair. I stand by my vote for B to ensure no single household bears the permanent burden.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, I know the frontage is unfair, but Option B just moves the truck noise to my door! I can't wait four months for C. I'm voting B to escape the gate!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, I understand the noise is urgent. But Option C’s subsidy covers forty percent, and it stops the thirty-four thousand yen in waste. I’m voting C to protect our shared budget.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, Option B just moves the friction, it doesn't remove it. We need a structure that lets us coexist without constant negotiation. I stand by my vote for C.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,"@Asuka, I hear you on the frontage, but Option B means moving the point four times a year. That’s endless setup and cleanup. I’m voting C to stop the bleeding!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, Option B is the only arrangement that corrects the physical disparity. I stand by my vote for B to ensure no single household bears the permanent burden.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
